      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T13:41:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This still adds a newline after every call. Suppose someone writes C code like\n\n```c\nfputs(\"Hello \", 0);\nfputs(\"World.\\n\", 0);\n```\n\n(Or something equivalent, I\u0027m not sure what calls doing `fprintf` results in.) This would end up on two separate lines, when it was intended to be on one. Note that unlike `puts`, `fputs` is not supposed to add newlines.",
      "parentUuid": "eed48c9c_3ce2bf1a",
      "revId": "2ee0d84e855e64da1760bf32eb8ab65ac81fd91e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
